{"title":"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(nifty_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (nifty solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Rigor_Graph_Analysis)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Rigor Graph Analysis)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aa6efb035f7bb99e25c3c65752ba4530cc77d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ab+1}{a+b} &lt; \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"88\" height=\"39\" />. The maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9677407e8f6e20fd32ad74d487fdd2d272cf1259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^3b^3+1}{a^3+b^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"66\" height=\"40\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347a1d5586e82c832f61ea799d89945ed2837fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us call the quantity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9677407e8f6e20fd32ad74d487fdd2d272cf1259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^3b^3+1}{a^3+b^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"66\" height=\"40\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for convenience. Knowing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers, we can legitimately rearrange the given inequality so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is by itself, which makes it easier to determine the pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> that work. Doing so, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba7b7a7888c43583af8ddeba7a117bc346e6cdc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ab+1}{a+b} &lt; \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df003654f229858f938ea85cf883fe67be2d830.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 2ab + 2 &lt; 3a + 3b \\implies 2ab - 3a &lt; 3b - 2\\]\" width=\"367\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b69c2893aa2be826dbfec672f6da4ed62d54511.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies a &lt; \\frac{3b - 2}{2b - 3}.\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" /> Now, observe that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060baf8684fa0925a7c988f59eea8d539c179444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = \\frac{a^3 + 1}{a^3 + 1} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"128\" height=\"42\" />, regardless of the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we have the same result: that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/10822d6bcba37497c1628483b6298c5dbf921cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = \\frac{b^3 + 1}{b^3 + 1} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"127\" height=\"42\" />, regardless of the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, we want to find pairs of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> existing such that neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and that the conditions given in the problem are satisfied in order to check that the maximum value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nTo avoid the possibility that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we want to find values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a13da366a76e98b6861129d55c196939df2693fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3b - 2}{2b - 3} &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"87\" height=\"41\" />. If we do this, we will have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0b94c848a5868aff11d54e97e9b63cb03e1bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac{3b - 2}{2b - 3} = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"120\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and this allows us to choose values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Again, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer, and we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b4a5f389c4da2b8d2b22498db71d019317eb9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, we can legitimately multiply both sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a13da366a76e98b6861129d55c196939df2693fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3b - 2}{2b - 3} &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"87\" height=\"41\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54e25fb049ffec5805701cd39cfb4b57f4e5eb25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b - 3$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/49719e394ddc3ded90db7c822e90fca5b770e5b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b - 2 &gt; 4b - 6 \\implies b &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"211\" height=\"13\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246ec286b9641f91f9dfa14932e47171e2fad854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469542e0aadcbea40a297c7f302b3e1578d070c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />, so the only possibility for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging these values into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12f6d0f794620dcd1b0d1fe6e3c5503d8f9b91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = \\frac{8(27) + 1}{8 + 27} = \\frac{217}{35} = \\frac{31}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"218\" height=\"40\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac0dc60242c346f99a86fa9bb78653da269eff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac{4}{1} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" />. Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b3c27171aba2140505212ce5b912115d1cdd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> in for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> yields the same result of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e66848a417f4359429a7dc78912f4b7b49ebd38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{31}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, but plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f355a4e7ead000bd887d7d4582bb114f900f3252.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = \\frac{8(8) + 1}{8 + 8} = \\frac{65}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"153\" height=\"40\" />. Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e66848a417f4359429a7dc78912f4b7b49ebd38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{31}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> is the largest value we can have for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/1086ada14963ade2c0a1cdb5f746411b3245f9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 + 5 = \\boxed{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>(Technically, we would have to find that b &gt; 1 before dividing both sides of the inequality by 2b - 3, but otherwise this solution is correct)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28nifty_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(nifty_solution)\">Solution 2 (nifty solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (nifty solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e5925aa4114288d3ddfaefac9a400ee5f90dc7b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ab + 1}{a + b} &lt; \\frac{3}{2} \\rightarrow 2ab + 2 &lt; 3a + 3b \\rightarrow 4ab - 6a - 6b + 4 &lt; 0 \\rightarrow (2a - 3)(2b - 3) &lt; 5.\\]\" width=\"590\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e662cf33b006ba4829e8a25ffbe0db08475911.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a - 3, 2b - 3 \\in \\{x \\neq 2k, k \\in Z \\} \\rightarrow\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3768343f620b5d1ebcd9c09fa4e1491b53bdde59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2a-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17fb7c262add3344c13deece0652f42e0bc7afc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2b-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> each cannot be even or else <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> will not be integers\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13fc9a65969e63bc861a781a0cc20c0832cecfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2a - 3)(2b - 3) = 1, 3 \\rightarrow (2a - 3, 2b - 3) = (1, 1), (1, 3), (3, 1).\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c3794251183387b8f2c037cf54dc3c944d652c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a, b) = (2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2).\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb82a90b4a1c1ec70f07e0d0efa95ec4a3674b68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3 b^3 + 1}{a^3 + b^3} = \\frac{65}{16}, \\frac{31}{5}.\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/9196ce1d1ad2209776e43ab0a80f5ce4af90dd7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{31}{5} \\rightarrow \\boxed{036}.\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a4a393f3fe85686203bb149b570911722ce93b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1 \\rightarrow b=1, 2, 3... \\rightarrow \\frac{b^3+1}{b^3+1}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"273\" height=\"40\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5ac86cec251a4c394f7a7cc2f6a9c65dca6857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;31/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9677407e8f6e20fd32ad74d487fdd2d272cf1259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^3b^3+1}{a^3+b^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"66\" height=\"40\" /> to be maximized, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601b6395bade638e3c09750532188f66d6a1e4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ab+1}{a+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"51\" height=\"39\" /> has to be maximized. We simplify as above to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a355773287b591da64a8932cc96b05a69d4e8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ab + 2 &lt; 3a + 3b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ceaa5d5225157890a9fcbab2b340668af174bfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-\\frac{3}{2})(b-\\frac{3}{2}) &lt; \\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />. To maximize, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> has to be as close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> as possible, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/3829f449fb37887a376e826c6e38bb14f444c4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"41\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b3c27171aba2140505212ce5b912115d1cdd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and checking back gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> as the maximum or the other way around, which the answer is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a26678a4a259c27be77e0fb00c31bc0ca5057c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{216+1}{27+8} = \\frac{217}{35} = \\frac{31}{5} \\rightarrow \\boxed{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"232\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Guess and check a few values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> you will find two things. One, that the highest values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are the closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdbd19877c13d1755e01b54ba640f512c883a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Two, that the pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876b66789c31005ef23e41081d8f7c10137faaa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is the highest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />. So plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626beed3a7eee094ce4b6cf79a49d81669f72d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/26445cbbf2ca5cfd1ccd2b7bcbc5c4b2c9d49978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((2*3)^3)+1/(8+27)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"19\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a905c7f1f6e805be3b78f7c760aaec2e388544c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{217}{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e66848a417f4359429a7dc78912f4b7b49ebd38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{31}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa2f72c67fa4cf8d65992200e0702ea48d664c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31+5 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\nSolution by Helloitsaaryan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c6560b5662dee00a54f920d4c3c609261c1cbf45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\geq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. We solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> from the original equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3734ad92cb41fd77bc578c6613891e965c058f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac{3b - 2}{2b - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/0418bbd33f58076209c3f2f3148348cfb351521b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leq a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, we can solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38f86e5c194521b9abf8a10b111e9263b8b8e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; \\frac{3b - 2}{2b - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"86\" height=\"41\" />. Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/d/20d3d0977cec97caeb345c697d8ab5bb6fe0a8e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} &lt; b &lt; \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"177\" height=\"43\" />. Approximating values, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/7/d47cd39ef8f3276a63569de47fc1f82c80317837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq b &lt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124b8221e82e316c7b7054a5cc0813f265fd7249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />. Now, plugging back <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3734ad92cb41fd77bc578c6613891e965c058f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac{3b - 2}{2b - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> doesn't work. Thus, we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58262280e3c5cf8e2ba3e7d2832acffbf021d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\leq a &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db133033330c82ea126da37a3822246e6527dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />. Clearly, we can plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbbf34dd49f73967d4dd594d728924ef348ed324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b) = (2, 2), (3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" /> and see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea44bd62795a5d84c16a028ff4fb079a5cb8e63f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> gives you the maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e66848a417f4359429a7dc78912f4b7b49ebd38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{31}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cc18fdcde5f1bf8e7077d1b03552bcd51444643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Firstly, if we assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407f682abd81c4315568706c6619bf1c43f815b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^{3}b^{3}+1}{a^{3}+b^{3}} = \\frac{b^{3}+1}{1+b^{3}} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"178\" height=\"42\" />, which is not a fraction. Therefore, we know that neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> can equal 1.\n</p><p>Starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d81fb6651cb619608e07c5f972ae584119418d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ab+1}{a+b}&lt;\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />, cross multiply and move the variables to the right to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b81e74ee97e94477f296c1454b72daf1252bb216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ab-3a-3b&lt;-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"16\" />. After multiplying both sides by 2, Simon's favorite factoring trick (SFFT) is applicable, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/c/aec7700e103d388b6c5d91f64e6849aa5951e315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2a-3)(2b-3)&lt;5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />. Now, we assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Then we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> can equal 2 or 3. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, the only possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> value is 2, and there are no other possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc53b0797a12d17273b1496cdffc030ef0a77bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. So the possible ordered pairs for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a58271ee2fd01b393f19ce02800fca56e113a2c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2), (2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8790f46883a296366f038323844601dd2cde9ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. It is easily noticeable that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876b66789c31005ef23e41081d8f7c10137faaa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8790f46883a296366f038323844601dd2cde9ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> both produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c4c06ea2986f1a126fe146b478ad265d4113e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^{3}b^{3}+1}{a^{3}+b^{3}}=\\frac{31}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"116\" height=\"42\" />, which is the maximum value. We then add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7e12e392e4ed5e14caaf66ce8c1658e1b47c2a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31+5=\\fbox{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"112\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>~justeau9\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Rigor_Graph_Analysis.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Rigor_Graph_Analysis)\">Solution 7 (Rigor Graph Analysis)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Rigor Graph Analysis)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Aime_ii_2015_q8_s7.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/38/Aime_ii_2015_q8_s7.png/450px-Aime_ii_2015_q8_s7.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"420\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/38/Aime_ii_2015_q8_s7.png/675px-Aime_ii_2015_q8_s7.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/3/38/Aime_ii_2015_q8_s7.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05ce6b1b24021f7bac57083ccf3784d933cc20c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/1079bcf292bdc3dda7e042f1b07b4a62418d86cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. Then, the first inequality becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e496fdd3fab4bf93ed5a433c99994348b80a2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y+1}{x} &lt; \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05dcd9294f9954fd4f9e167dbf8d4b30999d970e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x &gt; 2y+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />, highlighted blue, and through the AM-GM inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea71802036237049def54d34f6d307e571051c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 \\ge 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, highlighted red.\n</p><p>For maximality to be reached, the points must lie on or near the quadratic, while in the blue region and red region overlap. Therefore, we can test points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c9416fca06e6dda6e9908f378c79c5da29ff993e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y) = (1,0), (2,1), (3,2), (4,4), (5,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"303\" height=\"20\" />. Note that every other point lies farther away from the quadratic starting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7da1b75cc1a945018db7316c26d618ca11ff9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, so no use in checking them. Also, the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/87182cdf9f3eb2525bec70dbbbb9a7f1af4fabfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x=2y+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" /> only intersects the quadratic at two points, and so afterward, values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> force the inequality too minor. We can manually plug and chug the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> into the requested result <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5caa3a7c988bdc223e664e9fc9899b4d284d0f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y^3 + 1}{x(x^2 - 3y)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"89\" height=\"45\" />, and see that the maximum occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/799d02a02fb177ab095513b6c692834f9fe62b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> (duh...). So, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83feb344f928847ad394c5605229661d5818c618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{217}{35} = \\frac{31}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />, which occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c2fc4c7597420a0d63734aa466d9da976fe11a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dcf06dd60e2c66af238981616d6d4cb9902ecb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9eb973aa01d2a44ff9f20aaaa8c2d64387b7545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re2qLzOKWk&amp;t=653s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re2qLzOKWk&amp;t=653s</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II\" title=\"2015 AIME II\">2015 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017052102\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.066 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.089 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 878/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28336/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.168      1 -total\n 59.90%    7.887      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.08%    5.014      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14135:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017052102 and revision id 285353. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}